# Autowrap (DECAWM), the pending-wrap state and how wide characters wrap.
#
# After a graphic character is written in the last column the cursor stays there with a "wrap
# pending" flag; the next graphic character wraps. Anything that moves the cursor clears the flag.

test text fills a row and the cursor waits in the last column
convention the delayed wrap (DEC "last column flag"): the cursor stays in the last column until the next graphic character; the programmer manuals only say the 81st character wraps
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij
screen
|abcdefghij|
cursor 1,10
wrapped 1 no

test the next character wraps to the following row
spec VT100 Technical Manual, Wraparound: the 81st character of a line is placed in the first position of the next line; VT510 DECAWM
size 10 4
feed abcdefghijk
screen
|abcdefghij|
|k         |
cursor 2,2
wrapped 1 yes
wrapped 2 no

test a line feed clears the pending wrap
convention a cursor movement control clears the delayed wrap flag, so a character after LF lands in the last column of the next row
known-fail: alacritty – LF does not clear the pending wrap: the next character wraps first
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\nX
screen
|abcdefghij|
|         X|
cursor 2,10

test carriage return clears the pending wrap
convention a cursor movement control clears the delayed wrap flag
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\rX
screen
|Xbcdefghij|
cursor 1,2

test cursor position clears the pending wrap
convention a cursor movement control clears the delayed wrap flag
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[1;10HX
screen
|abcdefghiX|
cursor 1,10

test cursor back clears the pending wrap
convention a cursor movement control clears the delayed wrap flag; the cursor is in the last column, CUB 1 puts it one to the left
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[DX
screen
|abcdefghXj|
cursor 1,10

test cursor up clears the pending wrap
convention a cursor movement control clears the delayed wrap flag
size 10 4
feed \e[2;1Habcdefghij\e[AX
screen
|         X|
|abcdefghij|
cursor 1,10

test autowrap off keeps the cursor in the last column and overwrites it
spec VT100 Technical Manual, Wraparound: without it the 81st and following characters overwrite the last position; VT510 DECAWM reset
size 10 4
feed \e[?7labcdefghijk
screen
|abcdefghik|
cursor 1,10
wrapped 1 no

test autowrap can be switched back on
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI ? 7 h sets DECAWM; VT510 DECAWM
size 10 4
feed \e[?7l\e[?7habcdefghijk
screen
|abcdefghij|
|k         |

test wrapping on the last row scrolls the screen
spec VT510 DECAWM: the text on the page scrolls up if the cursor is at the end of the scrolling region
size 10 4
feed \e[4;1Habcdefghijkl
screen
|          |
|          |
|abcdefghij|
|kl        |
wrapped 3 yes
cursor 4,3

test a full last row does not scroll until the next character
spec VT100 Technical Manual, Wraparound: the scroll happens with the 81st character
size 10 4
feed \e[4;1Habcdefghij
screen
|          |
|          |
|          |
|abcdefghij|
cursor 4,10
scrollback-len 0

test a line feed in the pending state on the last row scrolls once
convention a cursor movement control clears the delayed wrap flag; LF at the bottom margin scrolls once
known-fail: alacritty – LF does not clear the pending wrap: the next character wraps first
size 10 4
feed \e[4;1Habcdefghij\nX
screen
|          |
|          |
|abcdefghij|
|         X|
cursor 4,10

test two full rows leave the screen unscrolled
spec VT100 Technical Manual, Wraparound: the 81st character is the one that wraps
size 10 2
feed abcdefghijklmnopqrst
screen
|abcdefghij|
|klmnopqrst|
cursor 2,10
scrollback-len 0

test one more character pushes the first row into the history
spec VT510 DECAWM: the page scrolls up when the character wraps at the bottom
size 10 2
feed abcdefghijklmnopqrstu
screen
|klmnopqrst|
|u         |
scrollback
|abcdefghij|

test a wide character that does not fit wraps as a whole
convention a double-width character (UAX #11 W/F) never straddles the margin; it wraps whole and the row is marked wrapped
size 10 4
feed abcdefghi日
screen
|abcdefghi |
|日        |
cursor 2,3
wrapped 1 yes
cell 1,10 text=\s width=1
cell 2,1 text=日 width=2
cell 2,2 width=0

test a wide character that fits exactly leaves the cursor waiting
convention the delayed wrap (DEC "last column flag"): the cursor stays in the last column until the next graphic character; the programmer manuals only say the 81st character wraps
size 10 4
feed abcdefgh日
screen
|abcdefgh日|
cursor 1,10
cell 1,9 text=日 width=2
cell 1,10 width=0
wrapped 1 no

test the character after a wide one in the last columns wraps
convention the delayed wrap (DEC "last column flag"): the cursor stays in the last column until the next graphic character; the programmer manuals only say the 81st character wraps
size 10 4
feed abcdefgh日x
screen
|abcdefgh日|
|x         |
cursor 2,2

test soft wrapped and hard ended rows are told apart
convention a row that continues because of autowrap is marked, one ended by CR LF is not (needed to rejoin lines on resize and copy)
size 10 4
feed abcdefghijk\r\nlm
wrapped 1 yes
wrapped 2 no
wrapped 3 no

test a tab at the last column leaves a pending wrap
convention HT does not wrap and, with nowhere to go, does not move the cursor, so the delayed wrap is still due (the behaviour the xterm-compatible suites expect of a program that draws to the end of a row and then sends a tab)
known-fail: alacritty – the tab wraps the line
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\tX
screen
|abcdefghij|
|X         |
cursor 2,2

test a tab with 'more fix' on wraps first
convention xterm's private mode 41 (ctlseqs: "DECSET 41: more(1) fix"): a tab with the wrap pending wraps, then goes to the next stop
known-fail: alacritty – no mode 41
size 20 4
feed \e[?41habcdefghijklmnopqrst\tX
screen
|abcdefghijklmnopqrst|
|        X           |
cursor 2,10

test a line that wraps after a space keeps the space when the rows are joined
convention a blank at the end of a wrapped row is text the program wrote (autowrap, DEC "last column flag"); only the end of a line is trimmed
size 5 4
feed abcd efgh
lines
|abcd efgh|
screen
|abcd |
|efgh|
wrapped 1 yes

test a line that wraps after a space keeps it in the history too
convention the history holds the rows as they were, so a blank before a wrap is kept there as well
size 5 2
feed abcd efgh ijkl
lines
|abcd efgh ijkl|
scrollback-len 1
